he Secretary of the Treasury to make loans, loan guarantees, and other investments in support of eligible businesses, States, and municipalities and to provide the subsidy amounts necessary for such loans, loan guarantees, and other investments in accordance with the provisions of the Federal Credit Reform Act of 1990 (2 U.S.C. 661 et seq.). The CARES Act appropriation is used to fund the credit subsidy portion of loans, loan guarantees, and other investments authorized under section 4003 of the CARES Act, and the remaining portion of such disbursements is funded by borrowings from Treasury through the Bureau of Fiscal Service. This appropriated balance and borrowings from Treasury are held as a fund balance with Treasury until disbursed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1096, 798, 1466], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"On December 27, 2020, the Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021, rescinded $429 billion of the $500 billion appropriation provided to Treasury under Section 4027 of the CARES Act. As a result, the Fund Balance with Treasury was reduced, from $480 billion as of September 30, 2020 to $51 billion as of December 31, 2020. Further, the Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021 provided that the remaining unobligated appropriation as of January 9, 2021 be rescinded as of that date other than with respect to those funds made available for administrative expenses pursuant to Section 4003(f), for the Special Inspector General for Pandemic Recovery pursuant to Section 4018(g), and for the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 266, 1488, 328], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Congressional Oversight Commission pursuant to Section 4020.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 328, 1490, 667], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Resources of the fund include (a) Fund Balance, which reflects the appropriation from the CARES Act minus the subsequent rescission of funds resulting from the passage of the Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021, the subsidy portion of investments and loans receivable and expenditures for administrative expenses in support of the CARES Act, (b) U.S. Government securities (dollar balances), (c) special drawing rights -SDRs, and (d) foreign currencies. Principal sources of income + or loss -- for the fund are profits + or losses -- on SDRs and foreign exchange, interest earned on U.S Government and foreign securities, and SDRs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 674, 1490, 1162], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-1 presents the assets, liabilities, and capital of the fund. The figures are in U.S. dollars. Amounts and transactions pertaining to foreign currencies have been converted to U.S. dollars based on current exchange rates computed according to the accrual method of accounting. Investments and loans receivable are reported at cost. The capital account represents the original capital appropriated to the fund by Congress of $2 billion, minus a subsequent transfer of $1.8 billion to pay for the initial U.S. quota subscription to the International Monetary Fund. The additional appropriated capital represents the $500 billion appropriated under the CARES Act Sec 4027 minus transfers, expenditures, and a subsequent rescission of $429 billion resulting from the passage of Consolidated Appropriations Act, 2021. Conversion gains and losses are reflected in the cumulative net income -+ or loss -- account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 1174, 1490, 1447], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-2 shows the results of operations for the current quarter and year-to-date. Figures are in U.S. dollars computed according to the accrual method. \\u201cProfit +- or loss -- on foreign exchange\\u201d includes realized profits or losses. \\u201cAdjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations\\u201d reflects net gain or loss on revaluation of SDR holdings and allocations for the quarter. CARES Act related administrative costs incurred in connection with the loans, loan guarantees and other investments are accrued.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1558, 592, 1582], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"See Table ESF-1 and ESF-2 on the following pages.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1326, 1994, 1441, 2018], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"March 2021\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1452, 90, 1494, 134], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"71\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [372, 382, 1262, 420], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"TABLE ESF-1\\u2014Balances as of Sept. 30, 2020, and Dec. 31, 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [463, 429, 1173, 460], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury for Management]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 464, 1494, 1428], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Assets, liabilities, and capital</th><th>Sept. 30, 2020</th><th>Oct. 1, 2020, through Dec. 31, 2020</th><th>Dec. 31, 2020</th></tr><tr><td>Assets</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>U.S. dollars:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Held with treasury:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fund balance</td><td>480,643,983</td><td>(429,080,095)</td><td>51,563,888</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>11,169,942</td><td>(4,306)</td><td>11,165,636</td></tr><tr><td>Special drawing rights 1</td><td>51,732,943</td><td>1,209,102</td><td>52,942,045</td></tr