d></tr><tr><td>Repayment of principal debt</td><td>120,015</td><td>121,786</td><td>123,663</td><td>124,924</td><td>125,688</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on principal debt</td><td>90,169</td><td>103,221</td><td>116,448</td><td>129,432</td><td>142,126</td></tr><tr><td>Total outlays</td><td>2,790,299</td><td>3,069,180</td><td>3,422,606</td><td>3,809,818</td><td>4,229,699</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>399,326</td><td>399,326</td><td>399,326</td><td>399,326</td><td>399,326</td></tr><tr><td>Cumulative debt, end of year</td><td>2,309,870</td><td>2,188,084</td><td>2,064,420</td><td>1,939,497</td><td>1,813,808</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1773, 515, 1794], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Detail may not add to totals due to rounding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1375, 1994, 1486, 2015], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"March 2021\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1437, 97, 1490, 127], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"101\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [375, 207, 1257, 250], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 269, 803, 391], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund was established on the books of the Treasury on April 1, 1987, according to the Water Resources Development Act of 1986 (Public Law 99-662, November 17, 1986) (26 United States Code 9505).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 391, 803, 698], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Amounts in the Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund are available as provided by appropriations acts for making expenditures to carry out section 210(a) of the Water Resources Development Act of 1986, as amended by the Water Resources Reform and Development Act of 2014 (Public Law 113-121, June 10, 2014), the Water Infrastructure Improvements for the Nation (WIIN) Act (Public Law 114-322, December 16, 2016) and the Water Resources Development Act of 2020 (Public Law 116-260, December 27, 2020).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 698, 803, 1157], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The appropriations act for the Department of Transportation (DOT) for fiscal year 1995 (Public Law 103-331, September 28, 1994), section 339, waived collection of charges or tolls on the Saint Lawrence Seaway in accordance with section 13(b) of the Act of May 13, 1954 (as in effect on April 1, 1987). Legislation was passed in the North American Free Trade Agreement Implementation Act (Public Law 103-182, section 683), which amends paragraph (3) of section 9505(c) of the IRC of 1986, to authorize payment of up to $5 million annually to Treasury for all expenses of administration incurred by the Treasury, the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers and the Department of Commerce (Commerce) related to the administration of subchapter A of chapter 36 (relating to the harbor maintenance tax). Section 201 of the Water Resources\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 269, 1494, 422], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"Development Act of 1996 (Public Law 104-303) authorizes use of the Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund for construction of dredged material disposal facilities associated with the operation and maintenance of Federal navigation projects for commercial navigation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 422, 1494, 636], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"A summary judgment issued October 25, 1995, by the United States Court of International Trade in the case United States Shoe Corp. v. United States (Court No. 94-11-00668) found the Harbor Maintenance tax unconstitutional under the Export Clause of the Constitution (Article I, section 9, clause 5) and enjoined the Customs and Border Protection from collecting the fee on exports.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 636, 1494, 761], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The decision was affirmed by the Supreme Court on March 31, 1998 (118 Supreme Court 1290). With the tax on exports no longer collected, revenues have been reduced by approximately 30 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 761, 1494, 940], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The Secretary of the Treasury invests in interest-bearing obligations of the United States that portion of the trust fund, in his judgment, not required to meet current withdrawals. The interest on, and proceeds from, the sale or redemption of any obligation held in the trust fund is credited to the trust fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 943, 1494, 1127], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"The Code requires the Secretary of the Treasury to submit an annual report to Congress [26 United States Code 9602(a)]. The report must present the financial condition and results of operations of the fund during the past fiscal year and the expected condition and operations of the fund during the next five fiscal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1372, 1992, 1488, 2018], \"page_id\": 107}], \"content\": \"March 2021\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1444, 97, 1488, 123], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"102\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [474, 262, 1155, 330], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-4.\\u2014Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [627, 346, 1009, 368], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"[Source: Department of the Army Corps of Engineers]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 375, 1484, 867], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2019</td><td>$9,306,746,015</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Imports</td><td>1,115,275,706</td></tr><tr><td>Exports</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Domestic</td><td>65,522,632</td></tr><tr><td>Passengers</td><td>11,175,352</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign trade</td><td>117,850,379</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>139,468,270</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>1,449,292,339</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Corps of Engineers</td><td>1,568,682,099</td></tr><tr><td>Saint Lawrence Seaway Development Corporation/DOT</td><td>38,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Administrative cost for Department of Homeland Security (Customs)</td><td>3,274,000</td></tr><tr><td>Operating expenses, miscellaneous returns</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td>1,609,956,099</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2020</td><td>9,146,082,255</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [322, 955, 1310, 1025], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"Harbor Maintenance Trust Fund Expected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2021-2025\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 1032, 1086, 1063], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Source: Department of the Army Corps of Engineers]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1065, 1488, 1603], \"page_id\": 108}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2021</th><th>2022</th><th>2023</th><th>2024</th><th>2025</th></t